{
  "date": "2026-03-31",
  "period_start": "2026-03-01",
  "period_end": "2026-03-31",
  "title": "The community kept building",
  "summary": "March widened what people can make with Pollinations while making the APIs, accounts, and tools around those creations easier to use.\n\nThe app catalog grew across writing, learning, games, developer tools, and media creation. SPORE users gained the ability to submit apps, while catalog cleanup removed duplicates and repaired links.\n\nSuno music, new speech and text options, and image and video models from Pruna, Nova, Qwen, Grok, and others broadened the API. Image editing gained more reference-image options, and several routes and input formats were corrected.\n\nOpenAI-compatible image generation and editing endpoints joined an SDK update with transcription, uploads, and account helpers. Tool-call, vision, and streaming fixes made existing integrations less surprising.\n\nApp Keys gained clearer attribution and authorization screens, while community apps connected Pollinations accounts for generation and uploads. Spore and Seed moved to hourly refills, and checkout gained stepped Pollen packs.",
  "pr_count": 331,
